Now let me carefully analyze the refactor for behavioral changes.

### 1. `asArray` / `asArrayRuns` / `asArrayResult`

Old:
```js
function asArray(value) {
   if (!value) return [];
   if (Array.isArray(value)) return value;
   if (value.workflow_runs && Array.isArray(value.workflow_runs)) return value.workflow_runs;
   if (value.jobs && Array.isArray(value.jobs)) return value.jobs;
   if (value.result) return asArray(parseJson(value.result, value.result));
   return [];
}
``

New:
```js
function asArray(value) {
   if (!value) return [];
   if (Array.isArray(value)) return value;
   var wrapped = asArrayRuns(value);
   if (wrapped) return wrapped;
   return asArrayResult(value) || [];
}
``

One subtle difference: when `value.result` exists, the old code returns `asArray(parseJson(value.result, value.result))` — the recursion returns `[]` if it can't unwrap (falls to final `return []`). New: `asArrayResult(value) || []` — `||` on the recursion result. `asArray` returns an array, and an empty array is truthy, so `|| []` only kicks in when the recursion returns a falsy value — but `asArray` never returns null/undefined... Actually `asArrayResult` returns `value.result ? asArray(...) : null` — when `value.result` is falsy it returns null, `|| []` → []. When truthy, `asArray` always returns an array (possibly empty). So behavior identical.

Wait, edge: `value.result` = 0 or ''? Old: `if (value.result)` falsy → skip → return []. New: `asArrayResult` — `value.result ? ... : null` → null → `|| []`. Same.

### 2. parseTokensLine refactor

Old flow:
- `extractFaPayload(text)`; if non-null → parseJson → if valid usage payload → return fa sample.
- If `text.indexOf('Tokens') === -1` return null.
- regex matches; if none → null; else build sample.

New flow:
- `faLedgerSampleOf(text)` → null if no consumable fa payload → fall through.
- `if (text.indexOf('Tokens') === -1) return null;`
- `cliTokensSampleOf(text)`.

Identical. `faTokensSampleOf` identical field-for-field (intOrZero = parseInt||0).

Wait — one subtle: old `requests: parseInt(payload.requests, 10) || 0`. New `intOrZero(payload.requests)` = `parseInt(value, 10) || 0`. Same.

### 3. normalizeLogPayload

Old:
```js
if (raw == null) return '';
if (typeof raw !== 'string') {
   if (raw.result) return normalizeLogPayload(raw.result);
   if (raw.logs) return normalizeLogPayload(raw.logs);
   return JSON.stringify(raw);
